---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
---
<Journey chapter="memory" first="gone" title="Write it down" description="The window is emptied between sessions. A file in the project is loaded at the start of every one.">
  <Step id="gone" title="The window does not outlive the session">
    <p>A new session starts with <a href={url('journey/chat/')}>the empty window from step 1</a>. Whatever the agent worked out yesterday went with yesterday’s window.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="file" title="A file does">
    <p>AGENTS.md is a plain file in your project. The harness loads it into the window before your first word, every session.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="session" data-val="with" data-default aria-pressed="true">With the file</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="session" data-val="without" aria-pressed="false">Without</button>
    </div>
    <More title="Which file each tool reads">
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.contextFile" show="claim" /></p>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.codex.contextFile" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="grow" title="Have it write the rule down">
    <p>When it gets something wrong, tell it to add the rule. Then press again, and again.</p>
    <div class="row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-do="teach">Add a rule</button></div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Have the agent write the rule down">{`You just wrote the date as month/day. This project uses day.month.year everywhere.
Add one line to AGENTS.md so this does not happen again: what to do, and why.
Show me the line before you save it.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="skills" title="Skills wait on the shelf">
    <p>A skill is a longer instruction file. Only its name is loaded until a job needs it.</p>
    <div class="row"><button class="btn" type="button" data-do="skill">Ask for a PDF</button></div>
    <Next from="memory" more={[{ href: 'explain/skills/', text: 'Skills' }, { href: 'explain/connectors/', text: 'Connectors' }]} />
  </Step>
</Journey>
